# Android
#
# The whole folder is generated — `tool/setup.ps1` runs `flutter create` against
# whatever Flutter is installed and then applies the two patches this app needs
# (the INTERNET permission, and kotlin.incremental=false). Committing it would
# pin AGP and Gradle plugin versions that match one Flutter release and break on
# the next, which is the failure this arrangement exists to avoid. See README.
android/
*.apk
*.aab

